  "id": "DrugBank_DB00471 - MONDO_4784",
  "verbalization": "Montelukast, a leukotriene receptor antagonist, is implicated in the pathogenesis of allergic asthma through its role in modulating inflammatory responses. The evidence suggests that Montelukast may exert a therapeutic effect on allergic asthma via a chain of indications that ultimately lead to the disease. Specifically, Montelukast is associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis and Allergic Rhinitis, both of which are inflammatory conditions that contribute to the development of allergic asthma. These conditions are further linked to Flunisolide and Fluticasone Furoate, corticosteroids that are known to suppress inflammation and are used in the treatment of allergic asthma. The presence of these indications, along with the shared pathway of inflammation and immune modulation, supports the hypothesis that Montelukast may have a role in the management of allergic asthma. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Montelukast to influence the inflammatory cascade that underlies allergic asthma, although further mechanistic studies are needed to fully elucidate its direct effects.",
